        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "898a2285-4e5b-52b0-a8ad-aa8ccc6e4c8a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Desaga, Robert Wilhelm Bunsen, Michael Faraday, Georg Lunge, Ferdinand Cohn\n- Organizations: University of Heidelberg, University of Breslau\n- Products: Bunsen burner, laboratory burner\n- Topics: instrument making, electromagnetism, electrochemistry\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Faraday was an English scientist born on 22 September 1791 and died on 25 August 1867 who contributed to the study of electromagnetism and electrochemistry.\n- In 1855, Peter Desaga perfected Michael Faraday’s earlier laboratory burner design into the Bunsen burner.\n- In 1859, Georg Lunge graduated from the University of Breslau for work with Ferdinand Cohn after studying at Heidelberg under Robert Bunsen and at Breslau.\n- Peter Desaga was a German instrument maker at the University of Heidelberg who worked with Robert Wilhelm Bunsen.\n- Robert Bunsen and his laboratory assistant Peter Desaga developed the Bunsen burner as an improvement on laboratory burners then in use.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
